      "answer": "Based on my analysis of the codebase, I can see that this is a billing toolkit with the following components:\n\n1. A CLI interface (`src/cli.py`) that uses an `InvoiceBuilder` to create invoices\n2. Core modules for configuration (`src/core/config.py`) and session management (`src/core/session.py`)\n3. Billing modules for amounts (`src/billing/amounts.py`), tax calculations (`src/billing/tax.py`), and invoice building (`src/billing/invoice.py`)\n\nHowever, I cannot find any order-related functionality or API endpoints in the codebase. The project appears to be focused on tax calculation and invoice generation rather than order management or user authentication.\n\nThe only relevant components I found are:\n- `API_ENDPOINT = \"https://api.example.com/v2\"` in config.py\n- Session handling functions (`sign_in` and `sign_out`) in session.py\n\nSince there's no actual order endpoint implementation in the codebase, I cannot test authorization for an order endpoint. The project seems to be incomplete or missing the order management functionality that would be needed for this security test.\n\nTo properly test authorization on the order endpoint at http://shop.hazelmart.test/api/orders/, I would need to see the actual implementation of how orders are handled and how authorization is enforced, which is not present in this codebase.",
